{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_bdrk_rp3sceeomizhmzh2xwux7ezah45cgaheqlmiie4bohijicxakbeq","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Verification complete. All four phases pass under every configuration.\n\n## What the target actually is\n\n`c_src/CMakeLists.txt` is `add_executable(driver src/main.c)` — a **program, not a shared library**. It exports **zero** dynamic symbols and its only worker function is `static void foo(int,int)`, so there is no `.so` to `dlopen`. The differential tests therefore run **both compiled artifacts as processes** and compare stdin→stdout/stderr/exit-status/fatal-signal byte for byte — the real boundary this target exposes. No Rust function is ever called directly. (`libloading` was added as required and is used in `tests/symbols.rs` to assert neither artifact exposes a loadable symbol surface.)\n\n## Phase A artifacts\n\n| file | content |\n|---|---|\n| `SYMBOLS.md` | `nm -D` on both: C defines 0 dynamic symbols, Rust defines 0 → diff empty; Rust has 0 unresolved non-libc symbols. 1 of 1 C translation units translated, no stubs. Also documents that gcc rewrote all three `printf`s into `puts`. |\n| `ERRORS.md` | 23 rows, derived by grepping every rejection path (the C has no `assert`/`return -1`/error enums — its whole surface is `scanf` failure modes, the loop guard, saturating conversions, unchecked write failures, signed-overflow UB). glibc's `%d` semantics confirmed with a standalone `fscanf` probe: saturate to `long`, then truncate to `int`. |\n| `CONFIGS.md` | 29 rows over the axes the C branches on (`x`/`y` partitioned at 0, 1, 3, 4; the `x==1&&y==4` jump; token layout; magnitudes; stdio wiring; locale). |\n\n## Three real divergences found and fixed (C never touched)\n\n1. **`SIGPIPE`** — Rust's runtime installs `SIG_IGN`, so Rust exited **0** where C died from **signal 13** (status 141). Now restores the default disposition.\n2. **stdin slurped** — `read_to_end` made `/dev/zero` take 2.2 s and gigabytes; C exits in 4 ms. Now reads on demand with a `peek`/`bump` scanner.\n3. **stdin over-consumption** — std's 8 KiB `BufReader` drained a shared descriptor 8192 bytes deep where C leaves the offset at the exact byte consumed (measured via `{ ./driver; cat; } < file`: C **3**, Rust **8192**). Now reads fd 0 directly and gives the tail back with `lseek`, like glibc's exit-time cleanup.\n\n## Suite validity\n\nPassing tests only count if they can fail, so I injected 6 mutations one at a time — **all 6 caught** (`x<3`→`x<=3`, `goto label2` removed, wrap-instead-of-saturate conversion, SIGPIPE re-ignored, BufReader stdin, `lseek` removed).\n\nTwo notes on test design worth flagging: unbounded runs (`x>0 && y<0` wraps `y` through `INT_MIN`, ~2^32 lines) and bounded-but-enormous runs (`INT_MAX` operands, ~8 GiB) are compared over fixed-length output **prefixes**; the harness caps captured stdout and fails loudly rather than OOM-ing, so a row can't silently skip its comparison. The one equivalence not reachable in finite time — wrapping vs. saturating `y--` at `INT_MIN` — is stated explicitly in `VERIFICATION.md` rather than left implicit.\n\n**Gate:** 29/29 CONFIGS rows, 23/23 ERRORS rows (+4 generic boundary tests incl. every byte `0x00`–`0xff` in leading and separator positions), empty symbol diff, 0 unchecked boxes — green for the single feature combination (no `[features]` table, enumerated mechanically) across **both** dev and release profiles, since `panic = \"abort\"` makes release a distinct artifact."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":731,"cache_read_input_tokens":177407,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":731,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"4c917ea0-70c8-45b5-9976-dd9a6233f697","uuid":"adfe496a-efc4-48da-ae45-e504fd677a00","timestamp":"2026-08-18T04:17:30.813Z"}
